{
  "_readme": [
    "Screenshot manifest for the explainer. Key = storyboard screen name; file = PNG in public/screens/.",
    "source = where ./sync-screens.sh copies it from (path relative to the shasha repo; null = no capture exists yet).",
    "  This is THE mapping: after new screenshots land in the repo, `./sync-screens.sh` re-copies everything.",
    "TV captures: 1920x1080 PNG (app JVM screenshot tests). Phone captures: 390x844 CSS px at any scale (@2x = 780x1688).",
    "If a file is missing the renderer draws a labelled placeholder (title + skeleton), so the timeline always renders.",
    "units = px: focus rectangles [x, y, w, h] are in the capture's own pixels (size = [w, h] of the capture, top-left",
    "  origin); units = rel: relative 0..1. The focus ring, zooms and tap markers in the scenes read them from here.",
    "patches (capture px) are drawn over the capture: 'base' always, other keys when a scene asks (ScreenPatch). They",
    "  only neutralise details of the capture (the app's own focus highlight where our D-pad ring takes over, an error",
    "  line); ops: rect {x,y,w,h,r,fill,stroke,strokeWidth,feather}, band (ring eraser) {x,y,w,h,r,width,color,feather},",
    "  crop {src:[x,y,w,h], r, levels:[from,to]} (re-colours a region: from -> to, white stays white), qr {x,y,size} (the video's pairing QR),",
    "  text {text,x,y,size,weight,color,anchor}, icon {name,x,y,size,color,stroke}.",
    "Check a screen with: npx remotion still src/index.ts ScreensDebug out/s.png --frame=<index>"
  ],
